{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"telerobotics telerobotics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md","fileName":"Telerobotics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Telerobotics","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[XR Environments]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","Degrees of Freedom","3D User Interface","Latency","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"telerobotics telerobotics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md","fileName":"Telerobotics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Telerobotics","heading":"Telerobotics","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Telerobotics is the remote operation of a robot that is geographically separated from its user. Because robots act in the physical world and can have many [[Degrees of Freedom]], their control often benefits from a [[3D User Interface]].\n\nThe interface must map the user's input to remote movement and return sufficient feedback for safe, accurate control. [[Latency]], incomplete sensory information, and mismatches between the user's controls and the robot's capabilities can make the task harder.","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Environments","Degrees of Freedom","3D User Interface","Latency","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"telerobotics telerobotics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Telerobotics.md","fileName":"Telerobot